course: dictionary
lesson: 3203
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Engine can mean a machine that makes something move, such as a car, train or plane. It can also mean the front part of a train, or a fire truck. The words around it are the context, and they show you which meaning fits.
explain: «Dogs learn the sound of each car engine» means the machine in a car, because car is the clue. «Diesel trains carry their own engine» also means the machine that makes the train move. Try your meaning in the sentence to check it. If "machine that makes it move" fits, you have the right one.
explain: Two words together can change the meaning. A search engine is a website that finds things on the internet, not a machine with wheels. Read the words before and after the word, and ask yourself: does my meaning make sense here?
fact: An engine is a machine that burns fuel or uses power to make something move.
fact: The engine of a train is the front part that pulls the cars.
fact: A fire engine is a fire truck.
fact: A search engine is a website that finds things on the internet.
fact: Steam engines were first used around 1700, to do real jobs such as pumping water out of mines.
exercise: A plane has 2 engines. How many engines do 5 planes have? | *10 | 2 | 7 | 25
exercise: «Electric trains take their power from overhead wires or from a third rail beside the track; diesel trains carry their own engine.» What does engine mean here? | A driver who sits at the front | A rail beside the track | *A machine that makes the train move | A wire above the train
exercise: What is a fire engine? | A steam toy | A kind of fire alarm | A tall ladder | *A fire truck
test: «Dogs learn the sound of each car engine, and they hear a dog whistle that is too high for people to hear.» What is an engine in this sentence? | A wheel on a bike | *A machine that makes a car move | A sound that is too high | A road for cars
test: In the example, what job did a working steam engine need to do? | Flying in the sky | Making paper | Carrying letters to homes | *Pumping water out of mines
exam: What is a search engine? | A machine that burns coal | *A website that finds things on the internet | The front part of a train | A kind of fire truck
